    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` field, formatted `'<customerCode>-M<YY>'` where `YY` is the last two digits of the registration-date year.\n\nSince the membership number is derived entirely from fields the owner already carries (`customerCode` and `registrationDate`), I treated it as a computed read-only field \u2014 exactly like the existing `displayName` and `initials` \u2014 rather than a persisted, denormalized column. Two small changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `membershipNumber` read-only property to the `Owner` schema (next to `customerCode`), so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"membershipNumber\", expression = \"java(formatMembershipNumber(owner))\")` and a small `formatMembershipNumber` default method that builds the value with `String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", customerCode, registrationDate.getYear() % 100)`, returning `null` when either source field is absent.\n\nThis keeps the formatting logic in one small single-responsibility unit alongside the other derived-field formatters, reuses the already-assigned `customerCode`/`registrationDate` instead of recomputing them, and avoids adding a redundant persisted column across the four schema files.",
